'''Stass Allie''', a [[Force-sensitive]] [[Tholothian]] [[Gender|female]], was a [[Jedi Master]] who lived during the [[Republic Era|final]] [[Standard year|years]] of the [[Galactic Republic]]. She was also the cousin of Jedi Master and [[Jedi High Council]] member [[Adi Gallia]]. Allie became a [[Jedi General]] in the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] and gained a seat on the High Council of the [[Jedi Order]] late in the [[Clone Wars]] when Gallia was killed.

Allie would not serve on the Council long before her demise on the [[planet]] [[Saleucami]] during the waning [[Standard hour|hours]] of the [[Cloning|Clone]] Wars. Having received the command to execute [[Order 66]] from the [[Sith Lord]] [[Darth Sidious]], [[Clone Marshal Commander]] [[Neyo]] and a [[Unidentified clone lieutenant|clone trooper lieutenant]] opened fire on their general from their speeder bikes, killing her instantly.

==Biography==
===Early life===
[[File:AdiGallia-TPMChallengers.png|thumb|left|200px|Master Adi Gallia, a cousin of Stass Allie]]
Stass Allie was [[Reproduction|born]] on [[Tholoth]] prior to the [[Separatist Crisis]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> She was the [[Adi Gallia's family|cousin]] of [[Jedi Master]] [[Adi Gallia]],<ref name="Card Trader" /> who was born into a high-ranking diplomatic family on [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> Allie was found to be [[Force-sensitive]] and brought to the Jedi Temple on Coruscant to start her [[Jedi]] training.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> She specialized in the [[Force healing|art of healing]], which would later become an invaluable resource during the long bloody years of the [[Clone Wars]]. Like her cousin, Allie would also become a consular and rising star diplomat.<ref name="Card Trader" /> She was eventually granted the title of Jedi Master<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> and became a member of the [[Circle of Jedi Healers]], in addition to serving as an [[overseer]] of the [[Medical Corps]].<ref name="ForceCollection" />

Allie was present in [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine's]] [[Emperor's office|office]] along with other [[senator]]s and [[Jedi]] as the issue of whether Palpatine should take emergency powers was debated.<ref name="Episode II" />

===Battle of Geonosis===
[[File:JediCircle.jpg|thumb|right|350px|Stass Allie was part of the Jedi assault team on Geonosis.]]
After the [[Jedi High Council|Jedi Council]] received word that [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] and the Jedi [[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] had been captured by the the leaders of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] and the [[Geonosian]]s, resulting in a sentence to [[death]], Stass Allie was recruited by and joined [[Mace Windu]]'s [[Jedi assault team|Jedi strike team]] sent to rescue them. She and her fellow Jedi fought valiantly in the [[Petranaki Arena]] against the [[Separatist Droid Army]]. Most of the Jedi were killed in the ensuing [[First Battle of Geonosis|battle]], though Allie and others managed to survive long enough to be rescued by the new [[Grand Army of the Republic|clone army]] upon its arrival. The clones proceeded to escort some of the remaining Jedi off the planet while the rest were ferried to key spots on the planet via [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry|Republic gunships]] in order to lead the clones in the wider battle.<ref name="Episode II" /> She and [[Bultar Swan]], who she had been fighting back to back with, boarded the same [[gunship]] and were brought to the desert plain where the battle had spread to. The two shared a nod before they both charged forward to continue fighting the Separatist Droid Army.<ref name="On the Front Lines">''[[Star Wars: On the Front Lines]]''</ref>

===Jedi High Council===
Over the course of the Clone Wars, Allie continued to hone her healing skills even while deployed as a [[Jedi General]]<ref name="ForceCollection" /> and her diplomatic skills were tested as the Separatist threat loomed.<ref name="Card Trader" />

In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Date note">{{TCWcanondates|501}}</ref> [[Savage Opress]] killed Adi Gallia during a fierce battle and Stass Allie was invited to take her cousin's place on the Jedi High Council. Allie gratefully accepted and followed Gallia's footsteps. Due to her new responsibilities, Allie frequently appeared at Council meetings on Coruscant as a hologram from the various Republic worlds she was assigned to.<ref name="YaOUotF">{{EncyclopediaCite|Yoda and Other Users of the Force}}</ref>

[[File:Yoda7JediCouncil.png|left|thumb|Allie and the Jedi Council discussed Yoda's report on Operation: Titan.]]
Later that year,<ref name="Yoda Date">The third arc of ''[[Star Wars: Yoda]]'' features [[Agen Kolar]] on the [[Jedi High Council]]. "[[A Seat on the Council]]" establishes that Kolar replaced [[Eeth Koth]], who served on the Council during [[The Clone Wars: The Lost Missions|''The Clone Wars'': The Lost Missions]]. ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of "[[The Wrong Jedi]]" to [[19 BBY]]. ''Galactic Atlas'' also dates the beginning of [[Great Jedi Purge]], which includes the events of "[[Victory and Death]]," to 19 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]]. {{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-chronological-episodeorder|text=''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' Chronological Episode Order}} places ''The Lost Missions'' between "The Wrong Jedi" and "Victory and Death", dating the events of ''The Lost Missions'' to 19 BBY. Kolar was later seen on the Council during {{Film|III}}, the events of which ''Galactic Atlas'' also dates to 19 BBY, including the [[Operation: Knightfall|destruction]] of the [[Jedi Order]], limiting Kolar's tenure, and ''[[Star Wars: Yoda: Size Matters Not]]'', to that year.</ref> Allie was present at a meeting during which the Council heard Yoda's report of a devastating weapon known as [[Operation: Titan]] that would turn the tide of the war in favor of the Confederacy. However, the available information on the enemy project was insufficient and Obi-Wan Kenobi mentioned that Anakin Skywalker's forces had recently captured a [[Munificent-class star frigate|Separatist frigate]], suggesting that they sweep the vessel's [[databank]]s. Yoda agreed, deciding to go join Skywalker himself. The two Jedi followed their leads and learned that Operation: Titan involved the construction of a new droid army containing "[[megadroid]]s."<ref name="Yoda 72">[[Yoda 7|''Yoda'' 7]]</ref> Allie was later present via [[holocomm]] when the two reported to the Council that the megadroids were under construction on the planet [[Golatha]] and informed them that they planned to [[Mission to Golatha|destroy]] the [[Golatha factory|factory]] there before the megadroids could be deployed on the battlefield,<ref name="Yoda 8">[[Yoda 8|''Yoda'' 8]]</ref> a task that they were ultimately successful in completing.<ref name="Yoda 9">[[Yoda 9|''Yoda'' 9]]</ref>

Sometime after,<ref name="Date Note 2">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of {{Film|III}} as occurring in 19 BBY.</ref> Allie was present in the infamous session when Anakin Skywalker was granted a seat as the Supreme Chancellor's representative member and denied Masterhood status; she was later seen in the hologram meetings when Yoda was sent to Kashyyyk and Obi-Wan Kenobi to [[Utapau]].<ref name="Episode III" /> In the [[Standard day|days]] after the [[Battle of Coruscant]], Allie was preparing to depart the [[capital]] on a mission to send troops to the planet [[Felucia]], where Jedi Master [[Aayla Secura]] was stationed. However, before she left for Felucia, she was transferred to oversee clean-up operations on the planet [[Saleucami]].<ref name="Yoda and Other Users">{{EncyclopediaCite|Yoda and Other Users of the Force}}</ref>

===Order 66===
As leader of the [[91st Mobile Reconnaissance Corps]], Allie took part in [[Siege of Saleucami|besieging]] the planet Saleucami during the [[Outer Rim Sieges]].<ref name="BC 33" /> During this momentous time, Kenobi would kill Grievous on Utapau, Yoda would lead the defense of Kashyyyk, and Anakin would [[Duel in Palpatine's office|betray]] the Jedi, leading to his fall to the dark side, as well as the commencement of Order 66 and the beginning of the [[Great Jedi Purge|Jedi Purge]]. Allie was accompanied by the 91st Mobile Reconnaissance Corps led by the [[Clone Commander|clone commander]] [[Neyo]]. Unknown to Allie or any of the other Jedi, the [[Cloning|clones]] had all been created with [[Behavioral modification biochip|inhibitor chips]], forcing them to comply with the execution of [[Order 66]] by performing the extermination of all the Jedi across [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Episode III" />

[[File:StassAllieDeath.jpg|thumb|350px|Stass Allie was killed by her clone troopers at the end of the Clone Wars.]]
As the Order was played on their [[comlink]]s from Supreme Chancellor Palpatine, Allie, along with Neyo and a [[Unidentified clone lieutenant|clone lieutenant]], were patrolling the bleak and barren landscape of the war-torn planet on [[BARC speeder]]s during the mop up operation. She was caught completely off guard as Neyo and his wingman fell back and fired upon her speeder without hesitation. She was killed as the speeder exploded into pieces.<ref name="Episode III" />

===Legacy===
{{Quote|Allie! O'ra've! Caladastorous!|A mourner shouting|<ref name="MoF">''[[Reign of the Empire: The Mask of Fear]]''</ref>}}
In the wake of the Jedi Order's [[Great Jedi Purge|eradication]] and the [[Declaration of a New Order]] by the [[Galactic Empire]]<ref name="RotS">{{Film|III}}</ref> in [[19 BBY]],<ref name="MoFDate">{{MOFdate|1}}</ref> a procession of mourners gathered in [[Jedha]]'s [[Jedha City|Holy City]] to grieve the fallen Jedi. Cries mourning Jedi [[Saesee Tiin]], Stass Allie, [[O'ra've]] and [[Caladastorous]] were heard.<ref name="MoF" />

==Personality and traits==
[[File:StassAllie-GalacticFiles2016.png|thumb|left|200px|Stass Allie wielded a green-bladed lightsaber.]]
Stass Allie was a focused, stern, young looking woman with a desire to help others. She had [[Color|indigo]] [[eye]]s and dark skin contrasted with green highlights around her eyes, hands and forehead.<ref name="Episode II" /> As a member of the Tholothian species, Allie had a scaled cranium from which fleshy white tendrils drooped from her head.<ref name="TholothianDB">{{Databank|tholothian|Tholothian}}</ref> Allie was 1.8 [[meter]]s tall.<ref name="Allie" />

==Powers and abilities==
Stass Allie was talented in [[lightsaber combat]], having been trained to knighthood. Her sword skills were grimly tested when she survived the opening battle of the Clone Wars on Geonosis along with 28 others out of the original 211 other members of the strike team.<ref name="Episode II" /> While her swordsmanship was impressive, her talent for [[Force healing]] was more so. She passed down this skill to other Jedi, including [[Barriss Offee]].<ref name="Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> Like her cousin, Stass Allie was extensively trained in diplomacy and advisory skills, but when the Clone Wars called for the Jedi to serve as generals, she realised that she was also a skilled warrior.<ref name="Yoda and Other Users of the Force">{{EncyclopediaCite|Yoda and Other Users of the Force}}</ref>

==Equipment==
Stass Allie possessed a [[Color|green]]-bladed [[Stass Allie's lightsaber|lightsaber]] that she used during the Battle of Geonosis. She also wore tall tan travel [[boot]]s, a [[utility belt]], a white undershirt with white pants, a grey tunic topped with dark [[Jedi apparel|robes]]. Her head was adorned with a [[Tholoth headdress]] consisting of a brown fabric rim framing her face laced with interlocking thin chains which adorned her scaled cranium.<ref name="Episode II" /><ref name="Character Encyclopedia" />

==Behind the scenes==
The creation of the character of Stass Allie is in many ways a [[Retroactive continuity|retcon]] that took place prior to the release of any [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Attack of the Clones'']] products. The filmmaker intended to use the majority of Jedi High Council members in the film's climactic Battle of Geonosis; however, because most of the film was shot in Australia instead of England, local model [[Lily Nyamwasa]] replaced [[Gin Clarke]], who portrayed Adi Gallia in [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']]. She filmed all of her scenes wearing Adi Gallia's costume, but the filmmakers eventually realized that she looked too different from Clarke's version of the character, so they created a new character for the film, who became known as Stass Allie.

[[File:StassPTGN.jpg|thumb|330px|right|Stass Allie is depicted incorrectly.|left]]
After the death of Adi Gallia in ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'', in January 2013 the supervising director for the series, [[Dave Filoni]], stated that the animation team had created a character model for Stass Allie and that she was to appear in the show in a later season. This never happened, however.<ref name="Filoni RFR">{{WebCite|url=https://www.rebelforceradio.com/shows/2015/9/28/rebel-force-radio-january-19-2013-premiere|text=Rebel Force Radio: January 19, 2013 (Premiere)|work=[[Rebel Force Radio]]|archivedate=20230828084324}} {{C|46:15}}</ref>

In [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Revenge of the Sith'']], Allie was played by both [[Tace Bayliss]] and [[Nina Fallon]]. The film depicts Anakin Skywalker to be the one to utter the line "A partial message was intercepted in a diplomatic packet from the chairman of Utapau."<ref name="Episode III" /> However, ''[[Star Wars: The Prequel Trilogy – A Graphic Novel]]'' mistakenly depicts Allie as the one to have said the line.<ref name="PTAGN">''[[Star Wars: The Prequel Trilogy – A Graphic Novel]]''</ref> The reference booklet "[[Yoda and Other Users of the Force]]" states that Allie only arrived on Saleucami after its battle had concluded during the Outer Rim Sieges,<ref name="YaOUotF" /> but other sources establish she was part of the Siege of Saleucami proper.<ref name="BC 33" /><ref name="TCW">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Clone Wars}}</ref><ref name="Force Collection Neyo Light">{{ForceCollection|Clone Commander Neyo|star=4}} {{C|Light side card}}</ref> As such, "Yoda and Other Users of the Force" must be incorrect.

